    "question": "Explain the difference between RGB and CMYK, and when you use each.",
    "slug": "explain-the-difference-between-rgb-and-cmyk-and-when-you-use-each",
    "shortDescription": "2. [REPORTED / SOURCE-LISTED] | Fresher / Entry-Level",
    "sampleAnswer": "RGB is an additive color model based on red, green, and blue light and is used for screens and other digital displays. CMYK is a subtractive printing model using cyan, magenta, yellow, and black inks. A designer should work in the color space appropriate to the final output. A screen design can use RGB, while a print project normally follows the printer’s required CMYK workflow or color specification. RGB colors may not have exact CMYK equivalents, so important brand colors should be checked before production.",
