    "shortDescription": "7. [REPORTED / SOURCE-LISTED] | Fresher / Entry-Level",
    "sampleAnswer": "White space, or negative space, is the intentionally unoccupied area around and between design elements. It does not have to be literally white. It improves readability, separates related and unrelated content, creates visual breathing room, establishes hierarchy, and can make a design feel more premium or focused. Removing whitespace simply to fit more information can reduce clarity.",
