    "question": "What is the difference between Photoshop and Illustrator?",
    "slug": "what-is-the-difference-between-photoshop-and-illustrator",
    "shortDescription": "11. [REPORTED / SOURCE-LISTED] | Fresher / Entry-Level",
    "sampleAnswer": "Photoshop is primarily a raster/pixel-based image-editing and compositing tool, while Illustrator is primarily a vector-graphics tool. Photoshop is appropriate for tasks such as photo retouching, pixel-based manipulation, and image compositing. Illustrator is appropriate for logos, icons, vector illustrations, and artwork that needs to scale cleanly. They can also be used together in the same workflow.",
