    "question": "What are bleed and safe margins, and why are they important for print?",
    "slug": "what-are-bleed-and-safe-margins-and-why-are-they-important-for-print",
    "shortDescription": "15. [REPORTED / SOURCE-LISTED] | Fresher / Entry-Level",
    "sampleAnswer": "Bleed is extra artwork extending beyond the final trim edge so small cutting variations do not create unwanted white edges. Safe margins define an inner area where important text and elements should remain so they are not too close to the trim or binding. For example, a background color may extend into the bleed, while a headline remains comfortably inside the safe area. Exact bleed and margin requirements should come from the printer or production specification.",
